From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] accel/tcg: the record capability launches a recordable
 machine

A run that may record needs, from launch, what x-rr-begin-record can't
change on a running VM: rr-ready's one TCG thread, one vCPU, virtio kicks
as MMIO exits and an x86 TSC that keeps its rate under icount. The record
capability turns rr-ready on. -accel tcg,rr-ready=on alone still builds
that machine, for a replay, which needs it but not the capability.

With the capability, startup refuses, naming the capability and the
argument, a machine whose arguments can't be recorded: an accelerator
other than TCG, thread=multi, more than one vCPU, the replay blockers
(-snapshot, -rtc base=localtime), and vhost backends, which handle device
I/O outside the log. replay_check_blockers() moves to system/replay.h for
this, with a stub; vhost_has_dev() says whether a vhost device exists.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later AND MIT
Origin: new
